{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Unstable as water.</b> The impetuousness and the haste with which you hastened to display your anger — like those waters that rush to their flow; therefore" "<b>You shall not excel.</b> You shall not have many of all those prerogatives that were fitting for you. And what is the impetuousness with which you acted impetuously? <b>For you went up onto your father's bed</b> —" "<b>Then you defiled.</b> That which ascended upon my couch — and it is the Shechinah, whose way it was to ascend upon my couch." "<b>Unstable.</b> It is a noun; therefore its accent is above, and all of it is punctuated with patach. And if it were a verb form, half of it would be punctuated with qamatz and half with patach, and its accent below." "<b>My couch.</b> A term for a bed — so called because one spreads it out by means of blankets and sheets; and many are like it: ״אִם אֶעֱלֶה עַל עֶרֶשׂ יְצוּעָי״ (Psalms 132); ״אִם זְכַרְתִּיךָ עַל יְצוּעָי״ (ibid. 63)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:01.922130414Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}